    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math lessons by adapting to individual learning paces and styles. For example, they can generate practice problems tailored to a student’s weaknesses, provide instant feedback, and explain concepts in simple language. This makes math more accessible and less intimidating for diverse learners."
